"""AI attribution: this whole file was generated by Claude (Anthropic) in Claude Code, following
design decisions made by the author. See ATTRIBUTION.md for details.

P1 v0.4 units (plan sections 3-5): assets, seeded parameters, timeline scheduling and rendering.

A unit is a group of versions (single-line parts) or one episode. plan_*() draws the parameters with a seed (texts,
voices, clips, room positions, levels, gaps); build() turns them into absolute times using the real TTS durations
(sources, the assistant's speaking turns and the decision points); render() mixes each version at 16 kHz and checks
that versions are sample-identical (+-1 LSB) outside the spans of the sources in which they differ, reverb tails
included.

Positions (results/step0_v04/rir_positions.json, relative to each room): near, across, door. Speech level by position:
near 0, across -4, door -8 dB (+-1.5) relative to the speech reference; events, footsteps, door and cupboard sounds
at drawn levels relative to the same reference; DEMAND noise at a drawn SNR. The assistant's voice is not in the
microphone (no echo), except in the report-only echo subset; its TTS only gives the speaking times.
"""
